From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Register QSEECOM listeners the smcinvoke
 way first

Android's qseecom driver registers listeners with the smcinvoke variant
of the register command (QSEE_OS/LISTENER 0x06) and falls back to the
legacy one (0x01) only when the firmware does not support it. On the
Xiaomi diting (SM8475, QSEE 0x1402000) a listener registered the legacy
way is accepted but never called: uefisecapp keeps non-volatile UEFI
variables in memory instead of asking the RPMB listener (0x2000) to
store them. Register the Android way, keeping the legacy command as a
fallback for any refusal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -130,6 +130,13 @@
 	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_REGISTER	= 1,
 	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_DEREGISTER	= 2,
 	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_RESPONSE	= 3,
+	/*
+	 * Same arguments as REGISTER, but the listener is also reachable from
+	 * applications that call out through smcinvoke. Android's qseecom
+	 * driver uses it first and falls back to REGISTER only on
+	 * -EOPNOTSUPP.
+	 */
+	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_REGISTER_SMCINVOKE = 6,
 };
 
 enum qcom_scm_qseecom_tz_cmd_info {
@@ -2349,11 +2356,33 @@
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Register the way Android's qseecom driver does: smcinvoke-capable
+	 * first, so that applications reaching their listeners through
+	 * smcinvoke (uefisecapp's RPMB storage, for one) see it too, and the
+	 * legacy command if the firmware refuses that one. Android falls back
+	 * on -EOPNOTSUPP only; any refusal is taken here, so that a firmware
+	 * answering otherwise keeps the behaviour this driver had before.
+	 */
+	desc.cmd = QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_REGISTER_SMCINVOKE;
 	status = __qcom_scm_qseecom_call(&desc, &res);
+	if (status || res.result != QSEECOM_RESULT_SUCCESS) {
+		dev_info(__scm->dev,
+			 "qseecom: smcinvoke listener registration refused (%d, %llu), using the legacy command\n",
+			 status, (unsigned long long)res.result);
+		desc.cmd = QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_REGISTER;
+		memset(&res, 0, sizeof(res));
+		status = __qcom_scm_qseecom_call(&desc, &res);
+	}
 	if (!status && res.result != QSEECOM_RESULT_SUCCESS)
 		status = -EIO;
 	if (!status)
 		list_add_tail(&listener->node, &qcom_scm_qseecom_listeners);
+	if (!status)
+		dev_info(__scm->dev, "qseecom: listener %u registered (%s)\n",
+			 listener->id,
+			 desc.cmd == QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_LISTENER_REGISTER ?
+			 "legacy" : "smcinvoke");
 
 	mutex_unlock(&qcom_scm_qseecom_call_lock);
 
